nternal/a2e-documents/src/front-components/document-browser.front-component.tsx` (1590 lines)\n- Component `DocumentBrowser` (default export `defineFrontComponent`, id `c31a0000-0013-4000-8000-000000000001`, name `document-browser`).\n- Recursive row component `DocumentTreeItem` (lines 1285–1534); wrappers `DocumentRow`, `DocumentSection`, `DocumentTrashRow`, `DocumentSharePanel`.\n- It is a custom tree, explicitly a \"sanctioned front-component escape hatch\" (comment lines 75–86): search, favorites, tree with drag reparent/reorder, trash, share.\n\n**How the tree is built (lazy, parent-keyed state):** lines 237–416.\n- State: `childrenByParentId: Map<string|null, DocumentNode[]>`, `pageStateByParentId: Map<string|null, TreeParentPageState>`, `loadingParentIds`, `expandedIds`, `draggedDocumentId`, `searchInput`.\n- Query `fetchDocumentsPage` (lines 139–183) uses `new CoreApiClient()` genql `documents(filter)` — roots filtered as `{ parent: { id: { is: 'NULL' } } }`, children as `{ parent: { id: { eq: parentId } } }`; `orderBy = [{position:'AscNullsFirst'},{title:'Asc'},{id:'Asc'}]`.\n- Nested view rebuilt with `nestTreeFromChildrenMap`; siblings map with `collectSiblingsByParentId`.\n\n**Pure tree helpers (this is where unit tests live):**\n- `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/lib/document-tree.ts` — `buildMoveDocumentPayload`, `isDescendantOf`, `collectSiblingsByParentId`, `collectDocumentsByIdFromSiblings`, `buildRestoreDocumentPayload`, types `TreeDocument`, `MoveDocumentPayload`.\n- `.../lib/document-tree-loading.ts` — `nestTreeFromChildrenMap`, `mergeTreeChildrenPage`, `needsInitialChildrenFetch`, `hasNextChildrenPage`, `TREE_CHILDREN_PAGE_SIZE = 50`.\n- `.../lib/document-tree-keyboard.ts` — `buildKeyboardMovePayload`, `TreeMoveDirection = 'up'|'down'|'indent'|'outdent'`.\n- `.../lib/fractional-position.ts` — local port of `generateFractionalIndexBetween` + `buildAppendPosition` (sandbox cannot import `twenty-shared`).\n\n**Relation model:** `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/objects/document.object.ts` — self-relation `parent`/`children` with join column `parentDocumentId`, `onDelete: CASCADE`; sibling order via fractional `position` string (comment lines 20–24).\n\n**\"In page\" child list:** `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/front-components/document-page.front-component.tsx` lines 740–820 renders `Sous-pages` from `record.children.edges` with inline child creation (`createChildPage`) and an \"panneau\" side-panel button. It currently has **no drag/reorder** — this is the \"in page\" half of M8f.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Existing document mutation path (reparent)\n\n**Browser component handlers (the path to reuse):**\n- `moveDocument(...)` — `document-browser.front-component.tsx:562–600`: builds payload then:\n```ts\nawait client.mutation({\n  updateDocument: { __args: { id, data: { parentId: payload.parentDocumentId, position: payload.position } }, id: true },\n} as never);\n```\n- `moveDocumentByKeyboard(...)` — lines 604–636, identical mutation via `buildKeyboardMovePayload`.\n- Drop semantics documented at lines 560–561: drop **ON** a node ⇒ child (append last); drop **BESIDE** ⇒ insert at index under same parent.\n- Native HTML5 DnD payload key: `event.dataTransfer.getData('text/a2e-document-id')` (lines 1317, 1360, 1478).\n- `restoreDocument` (lines 688–713) also writes `parentId`+`position`.\n\n**Pure payload builders:** `buildMoveDocumentPayload` (`document-tree.ts:56–89`, throws on self/descendant) and `buildKeyboardMovePayload` (`document-tree-keyboard.ts:86–130`, returns `null` at bounds).\n\n**Server-side cycle guard (do not bypass):**\n- `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/lib/document-cycle.ts` — `validateDocumentParentMove`, `isDocumentParentCycle`, `resolveDocumentCycleRepairParentId`, `repairDocumentParentCycle`.\n- Mounted by `.../src/logic-functions/guard-document-parent-cycle.ts` (id `...0012-...0003`).\n\n**Native host hooks (context, NOT usable from the sandbox):** `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/hooks/useUpdateOneRecord.ts`, `useCreateOneRecord.ts`, `useFindOneRecord.ts`, etc. There is no `useUpdateOneDocument`; the app must keep using `CoreApiClient`/SDK. The US-157 note \"Reuses the document copy path (never forks it)\" means keep using these app helpers, not native hooks.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Existing document copy/duplicate helper (US-131)\n\nThere is **no recursive subtree copy helper yet**. The existing \"copy helper\" is single-record content copy with fresh block IDs:\n\n`packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/lib/instantiate-template.ts`\n- `remapTemplateBlockIds(blocknote, {createBlockId?})` — deep clone that re-keys every blocknote block ID, follows internal refs, **skips `threadId`**; returns `null` for malformed/empty. (lines 128–169)\n- `buildTemplateCopyPayload(source, {position?, createBlockId?})` → `{ title, kind: DOCUMENT, position, content }`, strips `Modèle — ` prefix; intentionally drops relations/system fields (`parent`, company/person, id, archivedAt, isFavorite). (lines 195–206)\n- `readAuthorizedTemplateCopySource(fetched)` — permission gate; null ⇒ fail closed. (182–190)\n- `buildTemplateCopyTitle`, `remapTemplateBlockIds`.\n\n**Template duplicate (single record, template kind):**\n`packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/lib/save-document-as-template.ts`\n- `buildTemplateDuplicatePayload(templateDocument, {position?})`, `buildTemplateDuplicateTitle` (appends ` (copie)`), `buildSaveAsTemplatePayload`, `buildSaveAsTemplateTitle`.\n\n**US-131 apply path:**\n`packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/lib/apply-template.ts` — `applyDocumentTemplateByKey`, `applyResolvedDocumentTemplate` (idempotent by `templateApplyOperationId`), reuses `buildTemplateCopyPayload`.\n\n**Other reuse of the copy helper:** `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/lib/record-note-copy.ts` (`remapNoteBlocks` calls `remapTemplateBlockIds`).\n\n**Implication for \"duplicate page copies children\":** you must add a new pure helper (e.g. `buildDocumentSubtreeDuplicatePlan`/`buildDocumentDuplicatePayload`) that walks the tree breadth/depth-first and emits one `createDocuments` payload per node with `buildTemplateCopyPayload`/`remapTemplateBlockIds` for fresh IDs and a `parentDocumentId` link; the browser already has `flattenNodes` and `nestTreeFromChildrenMap` to feed it. Requesting children may require a recursive query per node (the tree is lazily loaded — see point 1).\n\n**Generic duplication in the app:** `apply-template.ts` find-by-`templateApplyOperationId` is the idempotency pattern if you need one.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Side panel document surface\n\n**In the app (sandbox API):** `document-page.front-component.tsx:130–136` already does:\n```ts\nopenDocumentInSidePanel = (id) => void openSidePanelPage({\n  page: SidePanelPages.ViewRecord, recordId: id, objectNameSingular: 'document',\n});\n```\nimported from `twenty-sdk/front-component`. `document-page` child list exposes a `panneau` button (lines 809–816). **This exact pattern is what the browser should adopt for \"open in side panel\".**\n\n- `openSidePanelPage(params)` — `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/front-component/functions/openSidePanelPage.ts`; types in `.../globals/frontComponentHostCommunicationApi.ts:18–96`.\n- Modern routed variant (preferred; `ViewRecord` is marked deprecated): `openSidePanelPage({ to: AppPath.RecordShowPage, params: { objectNameSingular: 'document', objectRecordId: id } })`. Host handling: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/front-components/hooks/useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts:206–256` (`'to' in params` branch) and `:272–313` (legacy `ViewRecord`).\n- Other SDK functions available to the sandbox: `navigate`, `copyToClipboard`, `closeSidePanel`, `enqueueSnackbar`, `openCommandConfirmationModal`, `uploadFile`, `useUserId`, `useSelectedRecordIds`, `useRecordId`. Full list: `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/front-component/index.ts`.\n\n**Native host hooks (reference / naming conventions):**\n- `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/hooks/useOpenRecordInSidePanel.ts` — `openRecordInSidePanel({ recordId, objectNameSingular, tab?, isNewRecord?, resetNavigationStack?, openInTab? })`. Convention for all `useOpenXxxInSidePanel` hooks (see `hooks/` dir: `useOpenFrontComponentInSidePanel.ts`, `useOpenRichTextInSidePanel.ts`, `useOpenCalendarEventInSidePanel.ts`, …).\n- `useOpenFrontComponentInSidePanel.ts` — host hook that renders a front component in the panel.\n- Document object is configured to open in the side panel: `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/views/all-documents.view.ts` `openRecordIn: ViewOpenRecordIn.SIDE_PANEL`; `useCreateNewPage.ts` relies on it.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Document deep link / route\n\n- Route constant: `packages/twenty-shared/src/types/AppPath.ts`\n  - `RecordShowPage = '/object/:objectNameSingular/:objectRecordId'` (line 40)\n  - `RecordIndexPage = '/objects/:objectNamePlural'` (39), `Bureau = '/bureau'` (28), `DocumentShare = '/share/:shareToken'` (8)\n- Host builder: `getAppPath(AppPath.RecordShowPage, { objectNameSingular: 'document', objectRecordId })` (`twenty-shared/utils`; used at `useOpenRecordInSidePanel.ts:100`).\n- In the sandbox `navigate(AppPath.RecordShowPage, { objectNameSingular: 'document', objectRecordId })` (browser `openDocument`, lines 120–126; page `openDocument`, 122–128).\n- Sandbox cannot import `getAppPath`; the existing deep-link string helper is `buildRecordSourceHref(objectNameSingular, recordId)` in `.../lib/record-note-copy.ts:87–90` → `/object/${objectNameSingular}/${recordId}`. Note its type is `RecordNoteSourceKind = 'company' | 'person'`; for \"copy link\" add/loosen a document deep-link helper rather than reusing the narrow type.\n- Public share link (different from a deep link): `buildDocumentSharePath(token)` in `.../lib/document-share-management.ts:37–38` → `/share/${encodeURIComponent(token)}`, copied via `copyToClipboard` in the browser's `DocumentSharePanel` (lines 1049–1060). The guest route is registered in `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/hooks/useCreateRootAppRouter.tsx:62` and rendered by `packages/twenty-front/src/pages/document-share/DocumentShareGuestPage.tsx`.\n- For an absolute URL there is no SDK helper that exposes `window.location.origin`; the host injects `copyToClipboard` (host impl `useFrontComponentExecutionContext.ts:471–492`, uses `useCopyToClipboard`). So \"copy link\" should pass the relative `/object/document/:id` (or add a small helper + test).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Existing drag & drop primitives\n\n**Host `twenty-front` — dnd-kit:**\n- Installed: `\"@dnd-kit/react\": \"^0.3.2\"` in `packages/twenty-front/package.json:40`; transitive `@dnd-kit/abstract`, `@dnd-kit/dom`, `@dnd-kit/collision`, `@dnd-kit/geometry`, `@dnd-kit/state` present in `node_modules/@dnd-kit`. **No `react-dnd`/`react-beautiful-dnd`.**\n- Shared primitives dir: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ui/utilities/drag-and-drop/` — `components/DragDropItemSortableCell.tsx`, `DragDropItemDropTarget.tsx`, `DragDropItemSortableHandle.tsx`, `DragDropItemDropTargetSlot.tsx`; `sensors/PointerSensorWithSourceGuard.ts`; `constants/DndKitSensors.ts`, `DndKitPluginsWithoutOptimistic.ts`, `DndKitCollisionPriority.ts`; utils `getDestinationIndex.ts`, `resolveDropFromPointer.ts`, `preventNativeDragStart.ts`, `shouldPreventDragActivation.ts`, `getDragActivationConstraints.ts`.\n- Nav-menu DnD: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/navigation-menu-item/display/dnd/` — providers `NavigationMenuItemDndKitProvider.tsx`, `PageDragDropProvider.tsx`; components `NavigationMenuItemSortableItem.tsx` (uses `useSortable`), `NavigationMenuItemDroppableSlot.tsx`, `NavigationItemDropTarget.tsx`, `NavigationMenuItemInsertBeforeDroppableZone.tsx`, `AddToNavigationDragHandle.tsx`; hooks `useNavigationMenuItemDndKit.ts`, `useHandleNavigationMenuItemDragAndDrop.ts`, `useHandleAddToNavigationDrop.ts`.\n- Page-layout DnD: `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/components/dnd/`, `page-layout/widgets/fields/components/FieldsConfigurationEditor.tsx`, `PageLayoutVerticalList.tsx`, `PageLayoutTabListDroppableMoreButton.tsx`.\n- `DragDropProvider` usage examples: `CommandMenuItemWithAddToNavigationDragDndKit.tsx` (`useDraggable`), `CommandMenuAddToNavDroppableDndKit.tsx` (`useDroppable`), `drag-and-drop/components/__tests__/DragDropItemSortableCell.test.tsx`.\n\n**App front-component (sandbox) — native HTML5 only:**\n- `document-browser.front-component.tsx`: `draggable`, `onDragStart` (sets `text/a2e-document-id`), `onDragOver`/`onDrop` (lines 1312–1338, 1356–1369, 1460–1493). Drop-on-self = become child; drop-between = insert index.\n- Parallel example (subtask reparent, different app): `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-projects/src/front-components/task-subtasks.front-component.tsx:323–357` (`reparentTask`, `detachTask`; mutation `updateTask`), pure builder `task-tree.ts` + tests.\n- `a2e-documents/package.json` devDeps contain only `react`, `react-dom`, `twenty-client-sdk`, `twenty-sdk` — you **cannot** add dnd-kit without a platform change; keep native DnD.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Existing move-to / tree picker dialogs\n\n**No move-to dialog exists anywhere** (no `MoveTo` symbol; `Move to` strings exist only in `packages/twenty-front/src/locales/fr-FR.po`, not source). Reusable patterns to model on:\n\n- Native folder picker with search (closest analog): `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/navigation-menu-item/edit/side-panel/components/SidePanelEditFolderPickerSubPage.tsx` — `SidePanelSubViewWithSearch` + `SidePanelList` + `SidePanelGroup` + `SelectableListItem` + `CommandMenuItem`, filtered by `filterBySearchQuery`, selection via `useFolderPickerSelectionData`.\n- Filter/search helpers: `packages/twenty-front/src/utils/filterBySearchQuery.ts`, `packages/twenty-front/src/utils/normalizeSearchText.ts`, `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/hooks/useSidePanelFilteredPickerItems.ts`.\n- Side-panel sub-page